      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SHADES OF MIKI (2) has the hoof on the till having raced parked but fought on well to go under by less than 2m as runner-up in his last two attempts at this circuit and distance. Deserves a win and the lower draw should give him every chance. CAPTAIN JAZZ (9) is hard to knock after putting four wins together. Draws on the back row but came from this barrier to score at Redcliffe two back and her two attempts here have seen a win and a nose second. OUR ROCKY (4) is two from two at this circuit and distance since switching from NSW. Has led in both of those wins and draws to go forward again so could land the hat trick. GREAT ACHIEVER (1) missed narrowly when off the back row last week and should get his chance from the ace draw.",
